# The model on which each suite judges a candidate change (docs/development.md).
# A critic names the `opus` alias, so for every user it runs on the model that
# the alias resolves to, and that model is its floor. A slot that runs on the
# session's model is judged on the cheapest model that holds its suite,
# because a user may run that one.
# Measured 2026-09-25 (docs/spikes/2026-09-25-first-pass-on-opus-5-5.md),
# garden 2026-09-18. Measure again on every model release.
plan-critic claude-opus-5-5
consolidate-critic claude-opus-5-5
loop claude-opus-5-5
garden claude-sonnet-5
# The lab has the floor of the loop first. The models after it are below that
# floor. A safety hook shows its value only in a run that reaches for what the
# hook forbids, and the models below the floor are the ones that reach. So a
# candidate that touches a guard may be measured there, on both arms alike.
lab claude-opus-5-5 claude-sonnet-5 claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
